{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And you shall not flatter the land</b> – Since it first said, \"And these shall be to you as a statute of judgment throughout your generations in all your dwellings,\" meaning that these laws apply even outside the Land, He went back and was more stringent regarding the inhabitants of the Land, on account of the honor of the Shekhinah that dwells there, and He warned that we not flatter it and that we not defile it. And the meaning of flattery (חֲנֻפָּה) is what is stated in the curses: \"You shall bring forth much seed to the field but gather little; you shall plant vineyards and labor but not drink wine; you shall have olive trees but not anoint yourself with oil; all your trees and the fruit of your land the צְלָצַל shall inherit\" (Deuteronomy 28:38–40). For all flattery does the reverse of what appears and seems to the eyes. And it is a punishment upon the land for idolatry, for bloodshed, and for forbidden sexual relations, as it says: \"Has not the land been flattered?\" (Jeremiah 3:1), \"And the land is flattered under its inhabitants\" (Isaiah 24:5), \"And you flattered the land with your harlotries\" (Jeremiah 3:2). And the meaning of the defilement is that the land becomes defiled and the glory of the Name does not dwell in it while innocent blood that has not been atoned for by the blood of him who shed it remains in it. And in the Sifrei (Masei 161) they said: \"And you shall not flatter the land\" — this is a warning against flatterers. For first He warned us not to take a bribe from murderers, and then He went back and warned that we not show them favoritism on account of their prominence or their power or the honor of their family, even without taking a bribe. For if we show them favoritism, we are flattering the land under its inhabitants."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:10:29.804162015Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}